  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Financing Facility 2021 - 25</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Core support to GFF
Norad support includes:
- NOK 1.8 billion in grant support to GFF for 2021-2023
- Soft earmark within this NOK 100 million in matching grants to &#x201c;Innovation to Scale&#x201d; initiative, provided no other donor will do so. Additional allocation may be made.
- Soft earmark funds within the grant to cover the 2% diff. betw. the total GFF and UNICEF fees (5%+ 7%) and the approved fee by Laerdal Found. (10%)
Ensuring universal access to sexual and reprod. health and rigths is core.

By late 2023 the GFF supports 36 low and lower-middle income countries with catalytic financing and technical?assistance to develop and implement prioritized national health plans to scale up access to affordable, quality care for women, children and adolescents: Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Burkina Faso, Cambodia, Cameroon, Central African Republic, Chad, C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire, Democratic Republic of Congo, Ethiopia, Ghana, Guatemala, Guinea, Haiti, Indonesia, Kenya, Liberia, Madagascar, Malawi, Mali, Mauritania, Mozambique, Myanmar, Niger, Nigeria, Pakistan, Rwanda, Senegal, Sierra Leone, Somalia, Tajikistan, Tanzania, Uganda, Vietnam, Zambia, Zimbabwe.</narrative>
  </description>
